---
import Layout from "~/layouts/Layout.astro";

export const title = "Privacy Policy";
export const description =
  "Read the Lilos Growth Privacy Policy to understand what information we collect, how we use it, and your choices.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section
    class="relative flex min-h-[320px] items-center overflow-hidden bg-secondary pb-14 pt-14"
  >
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-secondary to-secondary-light"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl px-4 text-center">
      <h1
        class="font-heading text-4xl font-extrabold leading-tight tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/85">
        Your privacy matters. This page explains what we collect, how we use it, and the choices you
        have.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <section class="border-t border-gray-100 bg-white py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4">
      <p class="text-body/70 mb-6 text-sm">Last updated: June 15, 2026</p>

      <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none">
        <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Lilos Growth is the business name of <strong>Lilos Online LLC</strong> (“Lilos Growth”, “we”,
          “us”, or “our”). We provide websites, local SEO, and related marketing services for home service
          businesses. This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, disclose, and protect information
          through <a href="https://lilosgrowth.com">lilosgrowth.com</a>
          (the “Site”) and in connection with our services.
        </p>

        <h3 id="company-contact">Business details</h3>
        <p>
          Legal Business Name: <strong>Lilos Online LLC</strong><br />
          Business Name: <strong>Lilos Growth</strong><br />
          Website: <a href="https://lilosgrowth.com">lilosgrowth.com</a><br />
          Support Email: <a href="mailto:hello@lilosgrowth.com">hello@lilosgrowth.com</a><br />
          Privacy Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@lilosgrowth.com">privacy@lilosgrowth.com</a><br />
          Support Phone: <a href="tel:+18587222920">+1 (858) 722-2920</a><br />
          Mailing Address: <strong>1440 Columbia Street, Suite 909, San Diego, CA, US</strong><br />
          Support Hours: <strong>Monday–Friday, 9:00 AM–6:00 PM Pacific Time</strong>
        </p>

        <h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Information you provide:</strong> name, email address, phone number, company name,
            website URL, service interests, messages, consultation details, and other information you
            submit through forms, email, phone, or scheduling tools.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Client and billing information:</strong> contact details, project information, invoices,
            payment status, transaction records, and related business communications. Payment card details
            may be processed by third-party payment processors and are not stored by us in full.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Automatic data:</strong> IP address, browser and device information, pages viewed,
            referring pages, approximate location, timestamps, interactions with the Site, and diagnostic
            data collected through hosting, analytics, security, and performance tools.
          </li>
          <li id="cookies">
            <strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> small files, pixels, tags, and local storage
            used to operate the Site, remember preferences, measure usage, and understand marketing performance.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="how-we-use">How we use information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            To respond to inquiries, schedule calls, provide proposals, and deliver requested
            services.
          </li>
          <li>
            To operate, maintain, secure, troubleshoot, personalize, and improve the Site and our
            services.
          </li>
          <li>
            To process payments, manage accounts, send administrative messages, and maintain
            business records.
          </li>
          <li>
            To measure Site performance, analyze marketing effectiveness, and improve our offers and
            communications.
          </li>
          <li>
            To send marketing communications where permitted by law and to honor opt-out requests.
          </li>
          <li>
            To detect, prevent, or address fraud, abuse, security incidents, and legal or policy
            violations.
          </li>
          <li>
            To comply with legal obligations, enforce agreements, and protect our rights, customers,
            and users.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="sharing">Sharing and disclosures</h2>
        <p>
          We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal information for money. We may disclose information
          to service providers, contractors, and professional advisors who help us operate our business,
          including hosting and CDN providers, analytics and advertising platforms, CRM and form tools,
          email and scheduling providers, payment processors, security vendors, accountants, lawyers,
          and similar partners. These parties are authorized to use information only as needed to provide
          services to us or as otherwise permitted by law.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may also disclose information when required by law, to protect rights and safety, in
          connection with a business transaction such as a merger or asset transfer, or with your
          consent or at your direction.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cookies-analytics">Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We may use first-party and third-party cookies, pixels, and analytics tools to keep the
          Site functional, understand usage, improve content, and measure advertising performance.
          You can control cookies through your browser settings. Disabling cookies may affect some
          Site features.
        </p>

        <h3 id="cookie-preferences">Cookie Preferences</h3>
        <p id="cookie-preferences-anchor">
          You can adjust your cookie preferences at any time using
          <a href="#cookie-preferences" id="cookie-preferences-link">Cookie Preferences</a>. If you
          use a consent banner, this link will reopen it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in
          this Policy, including to provide services, maintain records, resolve disputes, enforce
          agreements, and comply with legal obligations. Retention periods vary based on the type of
          information and the reason we collected it.
        </p>

        <h2 id="your-rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            You may request access, correction, deletion, or portability of personal information
            where applicable.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can opt out of marketing communications by following the unsubscribe instructions in
            our messages or contacting us.
          </li>
          <li>You can block or delete cookies using most browser settings.</li>
          <li>
            You may appeal, object, or limit certain processing where applicable law provides those
            rights.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="california">Notice to California residents</h2>
        <p>
          California residents may have rights to know, access, correct, delete, and limit certain
          uses of personal information, and to opt out of “sale” or “sharing” as those terms are
          defined by California privacy law. We do not sell personal information for money. Some
          analytics or advertising cookies may be considered a “share” under California law. You can
          opt out of non-essential cookies by declining them in our banner or by revisiting your
          <a href="#cookie-preferences" id="cookie-preferences-link-2">Cookie Preferences</a>. We
          will not discriminate against you for exercising privacy rights.
        </p>

        <h2 id="intl">Visitors from outside the United States</h2>
        <p>
          We are based in the United States, and information may be processed in the United States
          and other countries where our service providers operate. Where GDPR or UK GDPR applies,
          our lawful bases may include performance of a contract, legitimate interests, consent, and
          compliance with legal obligations. You may contact us to exercise applicable rights.
        </p>

        <h2 id="security">Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect
          information. However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we
          cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2 id="children">Children’s privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our Site and services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly
          collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided
          personal information to us, please contact us so we can take appropriate steps.
        </p>

        <h2 id="third-party-links">Third-party links</h2>
        <p>
          The Site may link to third-party websites, platforms, or services. We are not responsible
          for the privacy practices or content of those third parties. Review their privacy notices
          before providing information to them.
        </p>

        <h2 id="requests">Submitting privacy requests</h2>
        <p>
          To submit a privacy request, email <a href="mailto:privacy@lilosgrowth.com"
            >privacy@lilosgrowth.com</a
          > or contact us using the details below. We may take reasonable steps to verify your identity
          before fulfilling a request, such as asking you to reply from the same email address or provide
          limited additional information.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">Changes to this Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top reflects
          the most recent changes. Your continued use of the Site or services after updates means
          you accept the revised Policy.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions or requests? Contact Lilos Growth at <a href="mailto:hello@lilosgrowth.com"
            >hello@lilosgrowth.com</a
          >, email privacy requests to <a href="mailto:privacy@lilosgrowth.com"
            >privacy@lilosgrowth.com</a
          >, call
          <a href="tel:+18587222920">+1 (858) 722-2920</a>, or write to 1440 Columbia Street, Suite
          909, San Diego, CA, US. Support hours are Monday–Friday, 9:00 AM–6:00 PM Pacific Time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
